ory for numbers, and also note that Candidate D shows strong responsibility, problem solving, and concentration, though has hot temper. Or we could argue Candidate A's anticipation and leadership are strong, but concerns about being a show-off and not open to new ideas. Need to decide vote. Probably we could shift to Candidate D? Let's weigh: B: conscientious, stress handling, weather, computer skills, but pretentious, nasty remarks, weak memory for numbers. D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but know-it-all, hot temper. Communication concerns also. C: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands tech, but egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education. A: anticipates danger, sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Long-distance pilot needs reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, crew cooperation, communication. B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues may affect crew cooperation. D has responsibility and problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew. C has quick decisions and calm, but egocentric and poor communication. A has anticipation and leadership, but show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nProbably B still strongest despite communication issues, but we could ask for more info on B's crew cooperation. Could ask Sarah for crew cooperation observations. But we need to produce a public message now. We could say: I agree with Emily's provisional recommendation for B, but note the concern about nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers, which could affect crew cooperation and attention to detail. However, given B's strong stress handling and conscientiousness, I still support B, pending clarification on crew cooperation. So vote for B.\n\nThus METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
